From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sim2hitl build <build@sim2hitl.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sensors: seed VehicleIMU integrators without a pre-sample interval

The previous sample timestamps start at zero. If simulated sensors start
seconds after boot, the first integration interval includes all that idle
time. Calibration then subtracts offsets over the bogus interval, and
EKF2 may accept a badly tilted initial gravity vector after clamping dt.

Use zero dt for the first accel and gyro samples. Integrator::put resets
and seeds its previous value at zero dt; the next sample therefore starts
the first real interval. Keep subsequent samples and saved calibration
unchanged.

Verified against PX4 v1.17.0 (d6f12ad1) with recorded SITL sensor streams.
---
 src/modules/sensors/vehicle_imu/VehicleIMU.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/sensors/vehicle_imu/VehicleIMU.cpp b/src/modules/sensors/vehicle_imu/VehicleIMU.cpp
--- a/src/modules/sensors/vehicle_imu/VehicleIMU.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/sensors/vehicle_imu/VehicleIMU.cpp
@@ -348,7 +348,9 @@
 		}
 
 
-		const float dt = (accel.timestamp_sample - _accel_timestamp_sample_last) * 1e-6f;
+		// The first sample establishes the endpoint; no interval exists before it.
+		const float dt = (_accel_timestamp_sample_last != 0)
+			? (accel.timestamp_sample - _accel_timestamp_sample_last) * 1e-6f : 0.f;
 		_accel_timestamp_sample_last = accel.timestamp_sample;
 
 		const Vector3f accel_raw{accel.x, accel.y, accel.z};
@@ -456,7 +458,9 @@
 
 		_gyro_last_generation = _sensor_gyro_sub.get_last_generation();
 
-		const float dt = (gyro.timestamp_sample - _gyro_timestamp_sample_last) * 1e-6f;
+		// The first sample establishes the endpoint; no interval exists before it.
+		const float dt = (_gyro_timestamp_sample_last != 0)
+			? (gyro.timestamp_sample - _gyro_timestamp_sample_last) * 1e-6f : 0.f;
 
 		_gyro_timestamp_sample_last = gyro.timestamp_sample;
 		_gyro_timestamp_last = gyro.timestamp;
